<bx:include template="../partials/_head.bxm">
<bx:output>
<div class="container">
	<div class="narrow">
		<header class="page-head about-head">
			<bx:if len( data.author.getAvatarUrl() )>
				<img src="#encodeForHTMLAttribute( data.author.getAvatarUrl() )#" alt="" class="about-head__avatar" width="72" height="72">
			</bx:if>
			<div>
				<h1 class="page-head__title">#encodeForHTML( data.author.getDisplayName() )#</h1>
				<p class="page-head__lede">Senior ColdFusion developer, BoxLang module author.</p>
			</div>
		</header>

		<div class="about-body">
			<p>I'm a senior ColdFusion developer who's been in the CFML trenches long enough to have opinions about all of it &mdash; from crusty tag-based components to whatever comes next. Most of my day job is stitching e-commerce platforms together (Shopify, Amazon, eBay, Walmart, and a few you've probably never had to integrate with) so that inventory and orders don't lie to each other.</p>
			<p>Outside work I build things nobody asked for. I wrote my own Express.js-style module for BoxLang because there were no alternatives, then used it to rebuild my own blog. I ported Zork.  When I'm not writing code, I'm reading Dungeon Crawler Carl, James S.A. Corey, or Rothfuss, min-maxing a City of Heroes build, or doing calisthenics because apparently that's a thing now.</p>
			<p>I like systems with real rules and earned progression &mdash; in games, in code, in most things. If it's held together with duct tape, I probably built the duct tape myself and documented why.</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>

<bx:if data.latestPosts.len()>
<div class="container">
	<div class="narrow">
		<section class="home-block">
			<div class="block-head">
				<h2 class="block-head__title">Recent writing</h2>
				<a href="/posts" class="block-head__more">All writing &rarr;</a>
			</div>
			<div class="entry-list">
				<bx:loop array="#data.latestPosts#" item="post">
					<bx:include template="../partials/postEntry.bxm">
				</bx:loop>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</div>
</bx:if>
</bx:output>
<bx:include template="../partials/_foot.bxm">
